The throwing gems to unicorns code is really weird and unintuitive.
Here's what it is now: (Spoilers)


                     co-aligned unicorn | not co-aligned unicorn
                   +--------------------+-----------------------+
identified gem     |        +5          |      -3 to +3         |
-------------------+--------------------+-----------------------+
unidentified gem   |        +1          |        +1             |
-------------------+--------------------+-----------------------+
identified glass   |        +0          |        +0             |
-------------------+--------------------+-----------------------+
unidentified glass |        +1          |        +1             |
                   +--------------------+-----------------------+

it seems to me that it would make more sense if it were something like:

                     co-aligned unicorn | not co-aligned unicorn
                   +--------------------+-----------------------+
identified gem     |        +5          |      -3 to +3         |
-------------------+--------------------+-----------------------+
unidentified gem   |        +2          |      -1 to +1         |
-------------------+--------------------+-----------------------+
identified glass   |        +0          |        +0             |
-------------------+--------------------+-----------------------+
unidentified glass |        +0          |        +0             |
                   +--------------------+-----------------------+

Just to be sure, I checked this out in wizard mode, and the top chart
is correct.
As it is, never identify your gems, and you can throw them to *any*
unicorn for a *guranteed* increase in your luck.

